    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s strongest plays today are headlined by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (80.87) and **Bryce Harper** (78.75), both of whom are set up for massive production. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a porous 5.13 xERA matchup against Merrill Kelly, with the optimizer rewarding his high-order spot and dominant SP-skill splits. **Bryce Harper** receives an elite boost from a favorable park factor and a solid 4.26 xERA matchup against Bradish; his 0.385 xwOBA expectation makes him our safest high-ceiling anchor. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) is our primary dark-horse play, leveraging a dynamic platoon advantage (R) and high park-factor projections to suppress his matchup against Montero.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Geraldo Perdomo** (44.54). While his ability to contribute in scarce categories like stolen bases is vital, he fell just short of the 50.00-threshold required to displace the high-efficiency projections of **Jonathan Aranda** or **JJ Bleday**. The optimizer prioritized the pure batting efficiency and positional leverage of our starters over the marginal gain **Geraldo Perdomo** provides against a tougher arm like Williams. We are also keeping a close watch on **Dylan Beavers** (52.50); while he remains in the lineup, his score is depressed by a difficult matchup against Zack Wheeler and the risk of being neutralized by an elite catcher\u2019s arm, which significantly caps his stolen base upside today. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the bottom of the order, specifically **Daulton Varsho** (49.66) and **Cal Raleigh** (49.31), both of whom are hovering near our \"Marginal\" threshold. **Cal Raleigh** is battling a negative park adjustment, and **Daulton Varsho** is struggling with a significant platoon disadvantage against Liberatore. While they are starting today, these players are on a short leash to preserve our seasonal game caps if they fail to produce early. We have **Yainer Diaz** 